  "spiritual_reading": "# Spiritual Translation of the Chapter\n\n---\n\n** ¶1. ** … the in most nature within … is the state of the mind in which … and … their ou termost boundary .\n\n**¶2.** What the inmost nature of this reality is — no finite understanding could re count or dis close, nor say in what manner it has existed from eternity — all things … and … dis close … eternity … great ness … and again the … tend toward … the origin of what is eternal and the boundary of what is eternal … that one is set down.\n\n**¶3. ** The state of spiritual death … the quality of the in most nature … which exists from ev erlasting to everlasting … within … with one another.\n\n** ¶4.** As for the perpet uity of evil and falsity which exists from the most ancient origin , no finite understanding is able to compreh end how they subs ist. For no other power was ever disclosed to them by which anything could speak or recount their origin or manner of existence. However, from the time when evil stirred itself and rose up against wisdom , seeking to come and dom inate the state of those who possess spiritual life —\n\n**¶5.** — the Divine Truth going forth to combat came out against it and held it back; he kept it separate from the interior mind where spiritual life dwells. He held it back . From that time, when wisdom was inter mingled with falsity, and spiritual life with spiritual death, it became possible to speak and to dis close how the assault and the spiritual conflict came to pass — how wisdom was entwined with fals ity — which is the ent anglement of life within death.\n\n**¶6. ** After evil stirred itself in its own in most nature, its intention … within its own state . It … the entire realm of falsity in its … of wisdom in the abyss of the lowest hell . For the inmost nature within it … because … they reckoned … on its side … this first quality of evil … because the external form of its nature was hard ened beyond any resistance that exists in the created universe.\n\n**¶7. ** … of spiritual death … envy, which is the hatred of all good … the realm of falsity … deliber ation within … wickedness … for as it … the injuries to spiritual life … against this realm of good and truth …\n\n**¶8.** Then he will rush … from the realm of … falsity. It drew away … his particular faculties … is deep … within them.\n\n**¶9. ** It spread itself throughout all things . It generated from itself five fundamental principles of evil: dense falsity arising from evil , self-love, reasoning from falsity, truth fals ified and inv erted, and utter negation of all good . From these it sprouted dist orted perceptions. It came up and formed itself within its own state ; it generated from itself by successive deriv ation in inn umerable emanations, none resemb ling another . In the deep est repositories of hell , it brought forth many evil affections — destruct ive impul ses, falsities born of the l ust for domin ion, and savage appet ites of every kind. It was established and grew powerful in the hid eous forms that belong to fals ity: dark , and by their fury , by their wickedness and mutual hatred, they destroy one another even as they war among themselves.\n\n**¶10. ** Then the deliber ation of the ruling evil humbled its own realm and all its powers. It perceived the nature of divine wisdom. It conspired to wage spiritual combat against the exalted kingdom of heaven and its glory .\n\n**¶11.** However , He — the Divine Love itself , the Father of all that is great — knew also of this war, of the intention to disturb the realm of wisdom. In the depth of His own divine wisdom He transformed Himself and went forth against it.\n\n**¶ 12.** Indeed , at that time … to go forth against … the Divine …\n\n**¶13.** From within itself it poured forth its nature into the fundamental principles of evil : into dense falsity, into self-love , into reasoning from falsity, into falsified truth, and into utter negation. It rose up from the deep est hell, establishing itself within dist orted perceptions that stood arr ayed against wisdom .\n\n**¶14.** Also , at the time when evil generated itself further , it formed works of its own kind , being established within them. Then the five external truths were summoned — the tru ths derived from the Divine Truth who goes forth to combat — the sons of the First Man.\n\n**¶ 15.** And at the time when evil generated itself from those works through its offspring, they fell into the natural mind and drew strength from the fundamental principles of evil and were nourished by them — wickedness together with cruelty — all concentrated within the ruling evil, the chief of all particular evils. He subjected his realms and his powers; he gathered them all into himself. He made himself ready for spiritual combat; he set himself to war against the state of mind illumin ed by wisdom, and against the great sovereign Divine Love who dwells within it.\n\n**¶16. ** At that very moment the Divine Truth going forth to combat drew near to his external truths — the divine principles that shine with their own light. He spoke with them, that he might entrust to them a charge ; he disclosed to them and taught them everything concerning what was to come . He assumed them upon himself. He arranged them in order. He cloth ed himself with them, one truth over another, upon his own fac ulties and powers — facing the danger — from the highest states of the mind — against evil with all its powers — from the beginning , it being beyond all measure .\n\n---\n\n* A note on method :* The \" five dark elements\" ( smoke, fire, wind, water, darkness) consistently correspond to the five fundamental falsities and ev ils by which the h ells operate : dense falsity obsc uring understanding , self-love consuming the will, sophist ical reasoning per verting thought , truth inv erted and falsified to serve evil, and the utter absence and negation of all good and truth. Their opposition by \" five garments\" corresponds to the five external truths with which the Divine clothes itself to enter combat — each one answ ering its opposite . The entire chapter describes , in spiritual reality , the process by which evil first st irs from its own nature, attempts to dom inate the regener ating mind, and is met by the Divine Truth proce eding from Divine Love, who clothes himself in accommod ated truths in order to engage in the spiritual combat that makes redem ption possible.",
  "reconstructions": [
    {
      "paragraph": 2,
